        try: click after the colon of total
        expected: only the formula is highlighted, from its equals sign to the end, and CHF 10.5 in front of it is left alone
    - D03 The Status Bar Shows A Hidden Formula
        area: cells
        fixture: the vat column of Ledger
        try: put the cursor in the vat cell of Agate, then click the formula in the status bar
        expected: the status bar names Ledger, Agate and vat and shows the column's formula; the click goes to the vat header
    - D04 Ctrl Arrow Jumps Only From A Highlighted Cell
        area: cells
        fixture: Ledger below
        try: click the region of Agate and press Ctrl+Right twice; then click inside 1,000 twice and press Ctrl+Right
        expected: from a highlighted cell each press jumps a cell and lands highlighted; from a caret it steps through the text, as anywhere in VS Code
    - D05 Ctrl Shift Down Then Shift Right
        area: cells
        fixture: Ledger below
        try: put the cursor on the amount header and press Ctrl+Shift+Down, then Shift+Right
        expected: the six amounts are selected, each whole, no pipe and not the divider, and the status bar says Sum 1,965 dollars and Count 6; Shift+Right adds the vat cells
    - D06 Typing Over Selected Cells
        area: cells
        fixture: the region column of Ledger
        try: click the region of Agate, press Shift+Down twice, type East, then press Ctrl+Z
        expected: Agate, Basalt and Cobalt all read East as you type; the undo puts them back
    - D07 Copy Into Excel And Back
        area: cells
        fixture: Ledger below
        try: select the amounts as in D05, press Ctrl+C and paste into Excel; then copy two rows of two cells in Excel, click the region of Ember and press Ctrl+V; then press Ctrl+Z
        expected: Excel gets one amount a cell, as numbers; the paste fills the region and amount of Ember and Flint, and adds no column
    - D08 Alt Down Moves The Selected Rows
        area: cells
